Z||000000||BAM-BAM||03-10-2000||09:42 PM||||  What exactly is the best, or prefered, way to flush and fill the Fiero engine cooling system. My 85 GT runs cool while the ambient temp is below 70 degrees, after that it starts to warm up. I might have some cap problems, and I'll relace those this weekend <BR>My radiator is new, and I'm not sure about the pump. However, like I said, it only starts up when the temp starts to climb. Here in Vegas we see our share of 110-115 degree days <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <P> Thanx Again,<BR> Bam  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||03-11-2000||11:36 AM||||make sure the fan is running up front. It should come on with the AC. If by some freak in vegas you don't have AC you probably should put in a switch to turn on the fan. Otherwise the fan only comes on when engine temp hits 235F.<P>That or order the low temp fan switch from Fierostore. ((I noticed Hypertech parts on either carparts.com or wrenchead.com the low temp switch may also be there.)) You do not need to change the ECM prom to use the low temp switch.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 03-11-2000).]||||reg||1
